<div class="mt-6 divide-y divide-slate-200"><div class="py-5"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900">Key data</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600"><li>Total NHS litigation cost: £3.6 billion (2018/19 data, referenced by Halligan et al.).</li><li>Radiology claims have increased in volume and value over the past decade.</li><li>Missed diagnosis is the most common allegation across all radiology claims.</li><li>Abdominal radiology claims have a high rate of incidental pathology allegations (37%, per Halligan).</li></ul></div><div class="py-5"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900">Implications</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">The rising volume of radiology claims reflects both the increasing centrality of imaging in clinical decision-making and the growing sophistication of claimants' legal teams in identifying radiological errors. Expert radiological review is now a standard feature of clinical negligence claims involving any imaging modality.</p></div></div>
</Section>
